from write_record import record,progress,ROOT
no_floor='The original defines no numerical 8x floor. All six organizational operations are executed below, with decision authority, incentive evidence limits, resource/process capability mapping, two structural alternatives, six routing trials, and a contrary-case repair; no numerical depth certification is claimed.'
record(1,'orgn',1,'Who can establish what in this research organization',
'Replace my undifferentiated picture of “the research program” with an authority and evidence map that changes how I classify and hand off findings.',
'I had the assignment as 51 named outputs plus a shared instruction. I could quote the boundaries, but had not represented which actor could produce which kind of evidence; “result” still denoted both a document and a change.',
'''
Organization: the current distributed research task; type: temporary research collaboration; scale: one integrating root and six assigned lines in the shared allocation. This application controls only representation files. The goal is to make a handoff usable without promoting a local construction into a human outcome.

The structure is hybrid: strategic scope and final saving belong to the root under the user’s request; local procedure execution belongs to each line; the user retains acceptance and future choices. Operational edits inside this line can proceed immediately. Cross-line integration depends on root review. Human trials cannot be performed by writing a case.

| Unit or role | Can change now | Can establish from current evidence | Cannot establish here |
|---|---|---|---|
| User | Request, acceptance, report of experience | What the user actually reports | Unreported comprehension or later conduct |
| Root | Shared synthesis, saving, final presentation | Existence and integration of supplied work | Independent validation merely by accepting a worker verdict |
| Representation worker | Local text, layout, classifications, later retrieval | The exact changed artifact and decisions using it | Model weights or human learning |
| Other lines | Their owned records | Their stated performed cases, subject to inspection | A result in this line without receiving its actual input |
| Source archive | Nothing; read-only evidence | Original instructions and supplied bytes | Faithful execution or useful benefit |

Stated values are execution fidelity, inspectable beneficial change, breadth, and honest unresolved outcomes. The observable allocation rewards coverage in the limited sense that completion is counted by named applications; there is no evidence of interpersonal rewards or punishments. A predictable structural conflict is count completion versus time spent on a difficult non-KEEP. That is a risk inferred from the count requirement, not a revealed psychological motive. The local record now has two separate fields: `application complete` and `reusable finding status`; completing an unresolved application will increment only the first.

Resources: original reader and file writes are strong; current-source provenance is strong; independent human participants and delayed observation are absent; shared instructions are available but dispersed; model evaluation is available but not independent; external sources can check facts but cannot supply evidence of this user’s response. Processes: source capture works for byte fidelity; substantive testing requires additional products; root saving centralizes persistence; deferred human outcome claims cannot be repaired by local confidence scoring.

Two viable structures were compared. A single centralized result queue gives the root one place to review all evidence and exceptions; it also forces local reader decisions through material the root has not yet integrated. A local evidence-qualified handoff gives the root scoped findings and links while retaining its authority. Local saving by every worker would duplicate a root-owned process and is outside this assignment. The adopted structure is the evidence-qualified handoff, with raw execution retained locally.

The new routing card is concrete:

1. Artifact or model decision observed in this line → local record, exact input and result, eligible for a local KEEP.
2. Human design without use → proposed intervention, UNRESOLVED human effect.
3. Report by another actor → attribute it and preserve its scope; no independent-evidence upgrade.
4. Source checksum → provenance evidence only.
5. Consolidation or publication → root handoff, never implied by local existence.
6. New contradiction within a KEEP’s scope → reopen that finding; outside its scope → preserve the old result and open a transfer question.

Six routing trials were then performed: an emitted source hash went to provenance; a completed format comparison went to local artifact evidence; a hypothetical quiet-room reading session went to untested human design; an existing root instruction went to authority; a future memory benefit went to unresolved transfer; a repaired table whose row dropped “reported” went to local repair with its original failure visible. The last trial prevents classifying every revised artifact as a successful first pass.

Capability assessment: this organization can preserve exact originals, build and inspect representations, and maintain scope-bearing local records strongly. It can estimate user choice burden only weakly without use data. It cannot verify durable human transfer in the present turn. The structural change is a small routing card rather than another review role; cost is one classification per handoff.

Certificate: exact claim—this authority/evidence map changes the disposition of at least one current candidate in this local workflow. Decisive case—the quiet-room candidate is now recorded as a design, while the source-hash candidate is excluded from behavioral evidence. Inference—the categories determine different verdict and reuse destinations, so the map changes operations. Strong contrary—the full shared instruction already contains these constraints; that defeats a claim of new substantive knowledge, but not the observed conversion of dispersed constraints into used routing. Unresolved—whether root review is faster or humans read it better.
''',
'My working representation now separates completion, provenance, local change, and human evidence. I applied it to six candidate dispositions and withheld two outcome claims that the assignment alone could not substantiate.',
'A local routing benefit is demonstrated: source authenticity and proposed human effects cannot enter the local keep set under the same label as a performed representation change. No human or root efficiency effect is measured.',
'KEEP — local evidence routing only.',
'The six-route card is preserved in routing-v1.md and will be the entry point for later dispositions. The raw source and full record remain available.',
'Test a report that mixes observed and inferred effects; compare actor-first and question-first retrieval; inspect whether a source update invalidates a result or only its proposed reuse.',no_floor)
(ROOT/'routing-v1.md').write_text('''Intended mind change: Route current results to the actor and evidence they actually concern.\n\n1. Artifact/model decision observed locally → local effect, exact input/result.\n2. Unperformed human intervention → proposed design; human effect unresolved.\n3. Another actor’s report → attributed report; no independence upgrade.\n4. Source checksum → provenance only.\n5. Shared integration/saving → root handoff.\n6. New contradiction within a keep’s scope → reopen; changed scope → transfer question.\n\nProvenance: 001-orgn-1.md.\n\nActual mind change: Used on six candidate dispositions in that record.\nBenefit: Local category separation.\nVerdict: KEEP — same finding as 001, no additional keep credit.\nOrganization: Actor and evidence routing; raw execution stays linked.\nNext attempts: Mixed claims and source-update cases.\n''')
record(2,'sim',1,'A short selector that retains its refusal and repair conditions',
'Turn the existing 11-step selector into a compact working sequence while retaining the conditions that change a decision.',
'The current selector is the full mind-change-selection.md: a valuable broad standard with 11 operations and a standards table. My default was to reread that whole selector whenever choosing a next operation.',
'''
Input: the complete current selector cited in working-instruction.md. Core purpose: choose and perform a useful next change, then update its reuse conditions from what occurred. Type: decision process. The audience is the model executing the program, not a novice human.

The component map retains every decision-bearing element. Essential: current request/context/capability; actor and locus; credible ordinary continuation; alternative changing the locus when the live choice is consequential; fit between operation and actual input; prerequisites and result-dependent order; benefits and total costs; authority to perform; actual execution; scoped consequence; revision or stopping; retained trigger and boundary. Supporting: the long enumeration of possible dimensions, examples of inferred purposes, and examples of costs. Decorative: none in the source is safely classified as mere style; the source is already functional. The simplification therefore removes examples from the working view but preserves their link, rather than pretending that a substantial cut proves superiority.

A first reconstruction was: “Choose a change, perform it, compare its result, retain what works.” Its missing conditions were tested directly. A relocation requiring the user’s action was falsely expressible as “perform it”; a sourced but untested claim was expressible as “works”; an expensive diagnostic was not constrained by total burden; a beneficial unchanged state disappeared. That reconstruction is rejected.

Corrected working sequence:

1. Recover the live concern, context, relevant prior correction, and available authority. Keep person, model, and shared conditions distinct.
2. Compare the strongest current continuation with a materially different viable change when that choice matters. Preserve a useful state when changing it adds no supported benefit.
3. Choose the operation and its locus from actual input, benefits, total burden, prerequisites, and uncertainty. Obtain a discriminating observation when its value warrants the cost; otherwise make a bounded reversible choice.
4. Perform the authorized change. A proposed human action remains a proposal until performed.
5. Compare what occurred with the intended effect and relevant alternative. Attribute reports and preserve competing explanations and unknown transfer.
6. Continue, repair, redirect, defer with a real continuation mechanism, or stop. Retain the situation, operation, evidence, scope, exception, and next-use trigger; check them at a suitable recurrence.

Preservation ledger:

| Original decision condition | Corrected location | Concrete test |
|---|---|---|
| Retrieve available context before asking | 1 | A source path is supplied: read it; no intake question |
| Compare with strong ordinary response | 2 | A clear answer needs no extra framework |
| Open choice of locus and representation | 2–3 | A dense table can become a verbal card rather than a stronger argument |
| Burden includes user choice, not only tokens | 3 | Six options require a recommendation when criteria support one |
| Result-dependent prerequisites | 3 | A keep must exist before it enters a consolidation |
| Authority and actual capabilities | 1, 4 | A reading-room design is unperformed |
| Report versus conduct versus transfer | 5 | “I understood” is a report, not delayed task performance |
| Repair changes dependent conduct | 6 | Removed qualifier is restored before reuse |
| Stopping and deferral | 6 | A future check without a mechanism is no scheduled action |
| Durable record is not guaranteed retrieval | 6 | Existing file still needs a future cue |

The six-step version was used immediately on the next representation choice: whether to add a diagram to the authority/evidence routes. The viable alternatives were a diagram showing six branches and the numbered route card already written. The card answers the concrete routing questions; a diagram would add no additional dependency information. Step 2 retained the existing card. This is a performed choice of unchanged representation, not a claim that all diagrams are wasteful.

Certificate: exact claim—the corrected six-step working view preserves all enumerated decision conditions in this finite selector comparison and can govern the next format choice. Decisive products—the ledger locates each condition and the next choice retains the route card under the ordinary-continuation comparison. Strong contrary—the longer selector gives richer prompts and could expose a neglected dimension; retained link and the requirement to reopen consequential uncertainty preserve that route. Unresolved—general completeness and user reading speed. The rejected four-verb version remains rejected despite being shorter.
''',
'I replaced routine full-selector rereading with the six-step working view, used it once to keep an already sufficient route card, and kept the original as the expanded source. The change is in reading sequence and selection conduct.',
'One unnecessary representation change was avoided in the local worked choice; all tested lost-condition cases remain addressable. No timing measurement or human comprehension claim is made.',
'KEEP — compact model working view for the tested selection conditions.',
'The corrected six steps, rather than the rejected four verbs, are stored in selector-view-v1.md. Exceptions and the source link travel with the compact view.',
'Test a case needing a sensory change; test delayed reuse with a different actor; compare a question-indexed view with this sequence.',
'The original has no numerical 8x floor. All five operations are executed, every decision-bearing input component is mapped, the first cut is falsified on four concrete lost conditions, the repaired output is tested against ten conditions and then used in a later choice. This is expanded execution, not a numerical eight-level claim.')
(ROOT/'selector-view-v1.md').write_text('''Intended mind change: Select a next change without repeatedly rereading the entire selector.\n\n1. Recover concern, context, prior correction, authority; distinguish person/model/shared setting.\n2. Compare strongest current continuation with a materially different viable change when consequential; preserve a useful state.\n3. Choose operation and locus from input, benefits, total burden, prerequisites, uncertainty; observe if worthwhile, otherwise choose boundedly.\n4. Perform the authorized change; unperformed human actions remain proposals.\n5. Compare actual effect with intent and alternative; preserve attribution, competing explanations, and unknown transfer.\n6. Continue, repair, redirect, defer with a mechanism, or stop; retain situation, operation, evidence, scope, exception, next-use trigger.\n\nSource and condition ledger: 002-sim-1.md. Full selector: ../../repos/perspectiveoptimizer/processes/mind-change-selection.md (workspace source; root integration can repair the relative link).\n\nActual mind change: Used in 002 to retain a sufficient route card.\nBenefit: Local next-choice compression with preserved tested conditions.\nVerdict: KEEP — same finding as 002, no extra credit.\nOrganization: Six working steps plus source-backed expansion.\nNext attempts: Sensory and delayed-use cases.\n''')
record(3,'ro',1,'Ordering an evidence record for inspection',
'Change my default source-first reading sequence into a defensible inspection order for a reviewer deciding whether a finding is reusable.',
'The archive naturally makes source-first reading attractive: skill source, comparison, application, finding, boundary, next attempt. That remains a strong order for checking source fidelity. The immediate reviewer task is deciding reuse, not learning the method.',
'''
Original list: S source, C comparison, A application, F finding, B boundary, N next attempt. N=6. Objective: expose what bears on a reuse decision early while retaining audit access. Type: inspection priority, not the authoring execution sequence. The first intent sentence is fixed outside this list. The scope-bearing finding must never be presented as unqualified proof.

Six dimensions, five-point scale; weights are explicit local preferences, not measured utilities. U decision usefulness (high=3); E direct effect evidence (high=3); D independence from earlier sections (medium=2); L limitation visibility (high=3); P provenance access (medium=2); R future action discrimination (medium=2). These separate functions: a source has excellent provenance but supplies no local effect, and a boundary has excellent limitation visibility but need not contain provenance.

| Item | U | E | D | L | P | R | Weighted total | Score basis |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| S | 2 | 1 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 1 | 36 | Verifies bytes; not the local result |
| C | 4 | 3 | 2 | 4 | 3 | 4 | 51 | Shows alternatives; requires target context |
| A | 5 | 5 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 | 61 | Performed input/result bears directly on use |
| F | 5 | 4 | 5 | 3 | 3 | 5 | 62 | Scoped outcome supplies the question answered |
| B | 4 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 3 | 5 | 60 | Disqualifying conditions distinguish reuse |
| N | 2 | 1 | 3 | 4 | 2 | 5 | 41 | Opens future work; does not establish this result |

The 15 complete pair comparisons use the total only as a preference guide. F>A by one: finding names the proposition whose evidence A supplies. F>B: a boundary needs a finding to bound. F>C: comparison needs the live question. F>S: local reuse differs from byte fidelity. F>N: completed result before unperformed future work. A>B: effect first permits the reader to understand what the boundary limits, but the scoped finding carries the key limitation immediately. A>C: actual result outranks predicted comparison. A>S: source alone cannot show effect. A>N: performed action before proposals. B>C: the veto condition is needed before importing comparative advantages. B>S: scope can disqualify even a faithful execution. B>N: present exclusion before future inquiry. C>S: contested causal/use comparison before detailed source audit. C>N: the existing alternatives establish what the next attempt must improve. N>S by raw score, but S is placed before N because the next attempt depends on understanding the retained source basis; this is a declared dependency override, not a secret score change.

Reordered: F (62), A (61), B (60), C (51), S (36), N (41). Movements: S 1→5, C 2→4, A 3→2, F 4→1, B 5→3, N stays 6. Confidence high on F before N and A before N; medium on B before C; low on F/A and A/B, which can move two positions when the reviewer has already read the finding. Most debatable: B; a known-result reviewer needs B first.

Complete sanity review: the top three all bear directly on whether reuse is justified; the bottom group supplies comparisons, audit detail, and future work, none dispensable. F/A/B near ties are resolved by proposition→evidence→scope, with the scope also attached to F so early stopping does not lose it. S/N is dependency-corrected. No authoring dependency is reversed: sources are still read before execution, even when displayed fifth.

Alternative orderings: source-audit task S,C,A,F,B,N; applicability task B,F,A,C,S,N; current general inspection F,A,B,C,S,N. Weight sensitivity: raising P from 2 to 5 moves S above N numerically and narrows its gap to C, but does not beat F/A because source bytes do not supply effect. Raising L to 6 makes B the first item (75 versus F71/A70), which is defensible for a transfer reviewer. Setting E to 1 lowers A relative to B and F, revealing that this order assumes effect evidence matters. These calculations are rankings of declared judgments; no claim of objective optimality follows.

Actual use: the next organization question, “Does local source storage qualify as durable program memory?”, was inspected in F,A,B,C,S,N order. F: no durability claim from scratch existence. A: exact files exist locally. B: root owns persistent saving. C: local receipt versus saved deliverable. S: supplied authority instruction. N: root handoff. The resulting disposition is a root saving dependency rather than a local claim of persistent memory. The source-first alternative reaches the same correct disposition; the changed order makes the claim and exclusion adjacent without measuring elapsed time.

Certificate: claim—F,A,B,C,S,N is the chosen general inspection order under the stated local dimensions and dependency. The full pair set and sensitivity show both the reason for it and the conditions that reverse it. Strong contrary—source-first is superior for archive-fidelity auditing; retained as a named alternate, so the general order is not universal. Unresolved—actual reviewer speed and preference. KEEP concerns the task-conditioned selection and use, not a fabricated speed gain.
''',
'I now distinguish authoring order from inspection order and used a reuse-oriented record order on the durability question. The strongest alternate order is retained for source audits.',
'The local reviewer representation makes the claim, its observed effect, and its disqualifying boundary adjacent; the performed durability disposition remained correctly limited. This is structural access evidence, not a human timing experiment.',
'KEEP — task-conditioned inspection ordering.',
'Finding→application→boundary→comparison→source→next is the default review route; source-audit and applicability routes remain explicit alternatives.',
'Test a known finding with a novel actor; give a source auditor the alternate route; replace any score dimension that proves nondiscriminating on later inputs.',
'Original 8x floor met: six independent-purpose dimensions, every item scored, all 15 pairs compared, every placement checked, three materially different orders, full confidence map, and three weight shifts. The numeric weights are disclosed judgment inputs, not empirical data.')
record(4,'orgn',2,'Stewardship for a reusable result rather than a pile of files',
'Change the representation line’s memory organization from file existence to accountable reuse with an explicit persistence handoff.',
'Files and receipts already existed, and the source-first archive made “recorded” look like a single state. Application 003 exposed that local existence, durable saving, and later retrieval are different states.',
'''
Organization: the representation line’s result-stewardship process; type: temporary knowledge-maintenance organization; scale: one local author, one root integrator, later readers not yet observed. Goal: preserve a result with the conditions needed for future reuse. This differs from application 001: the decision here concerns version identity and retrieval responsibility over time, not which actor can support a present outcome claim.

Structure and authority: the local author owns exact execution and local links; the root owns saving and shared integration; a future user of a finding owns checking the applicability trigger. Strategic target and evidence standards remain in working-instruction.md. The local author can repair local paths now; it cannot declare that a future reader will retrieve them. Fast local editing and slower cross-line integration are a dependency distinction, not measured clock times.

Stated values: correction and continuity. Revealed local behavior: originals were captured separately, and a compact selector was written with an invalid relative link to the previous selector. That actual defect is evidence that file creation alone does not establish usable access. The error is a path rooted one directory too shallow, not a psychological incentive failure. Count-based progress can overlook this because the file still exists.

Resources/processes: exact receipts support provenance strongly; stable application IDs support local references; scratch persistence is not a guaranteed resource; mutable navigation without version labels would blur what a later use actually read. Human episodic memory and future scheduling are not supplied capabilities. Source receipts and keep findings require different lifecycles: a source update does not retroactively change the bytes used by a historical application, while a finding’s applicability can reopen.

Two serious structures: (A) one continuously edited synthesis with links to the evidence; (B) immutable application records plus small versioned working views and a root-owned save manifest. A makes the current answer easy to find and minimizes duplication; B permits a later failure to identify exactly which scoped rule was used. This run chooses B because preserving revisions and exclusions is part of the research question. A remains a reasonable final reading surface, provided it links to B.

The implemented stewardship map:

| Object | Local owner/action | Reuse identity | Trigger for revision | Root handoff requirement |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Original source | preserve emitted bytes | source hash | archive version changes | retain exact receipt |
| Application | record actual input/output | numbered filename | failed claim or newly found defect | save complete record |
| Working view | use in later choices | view name + supporting keeps | better organization or lost condition | save with source links |
| Consolidation | only established keeps | numbered consolidation | four more unique keeps | save includes rejected organizations |
| Human proposal | preserve untested state | actor + intended task | actual trial arrives | never present as observed effect |
| Navigation pointer | local target check | exact relative path | movement or rename | fix delivery links after saving |

Applied repair: the selector view’s link was changed from `../../repos/...` to `../../repos/...` only after resolving the path would still be wrong; the correct local relative route from this directory is `../../repos`? Compute rather than infer: representation → mind-change-research → scratch, then repos. That is two parents, so `../../repos/perspectiveoptimizer/processes/mind-change-selection.md` is in fact correct. The suspected defect did not exist. The negative inspection result matters: a plausible allegation of failure is not evidence of a failure. No repair is claimed for that path.

The genuine organization change is a reuse ledger with separate local/durable/retrieved states. Six actual object entries were classified: originals local=yes; four application drafts local=yes; routing-v1 local=yes and used in application 003; selector-view-v1 local=yes and used in 002; consolidation not yet produced at this point; all durable-save states pending root. The implemented ledger refuses to infer “retrieved later” from “file exists”.

Capability outcome: strong local traceability; moderate cross-record navigation because the working views are explicit; no established durability yet. The structural workaround is a handoff state, not a second uploader. Cost is a small state ledger and the need to update it at actual use.

Certificate: claim—separating object existence, saving, and actual reuse prevents the present ledger from reporting unobserved durability or retrieval. Decisive entries—all existing local objects retain durable-save=pending; only two views receive actual-use references. Inference—the ledger expresses actual distinct outcomes instead of a single completion boolean. Strong contrary—an ordinary folder with links may suffice for one reading session; accepted, but it cannot answer this program’s requested later-uptake question without an equivalent state distinction. The attempted path-defect countercase failed and contributes no evidence of a repaired link. Unresolved—root saving success and future retention.
''',
'I now record three distinct states—exists locally, saved durably by root, and actually reused—and populated them for the present objects. I also rejected an initially plausible path-error diagnosis after resolving the path.',
'The current handoff can distinguish evidence that exists from evidence that has been used. This prevents unsupported continuity claims within the local manifest. No persistence or human memory improvement is claimed.',
'KEEP — accountable local reuse states.',
'The current object states are in reuse-ledger.json; versioned views point to unchanged application evidence. This finding is distinct from actor/evidence routing in 001.',
'Test a superseded view; test a result retained historically but rejected for a new scope; compare one current synthesis with the versioned substrate on a later correction.',no_floor)
import json
(ROOT/'reuse-ledger.json').write_text(json.dumps({'source_receipts':{'local':True,'durable':'pending_root','used_in':['001-orgn-1.md','002-sim-1.md','003-ro-1.md','004-orgn-2.md']},'routing-v1.md':{'local':True,'durable':'pending_root','used_in':['003-ro-1.md']},'selector-view-v1.md':{'local':True,'durable':'pending_root','used_in':['002-sim-1.md']},'applications_001_to_004':{'local':True,'durable':'pending_root','used_later':'not_implied_by_existence'}},indent=2))
progress()
